Greg thanks for joining us on short  notice how are you I'm well dan good to  be with you thanks for the invitation  well I've been talking about this the  last two days now on the show of is  there a way to extrapolate and maybe we  make it a a team play off and then how  do we get through all of the hurdles  here what do you think of the  possibility of of that happening where  we go from four to eight and how could  you see that actually working it is the  most frequently asked question of me  during my now four football seasons as a  conference commissioner so understand  that topic in my view will never go away  it has not been the subject of planning  strategizing here's where we go  among the commissioners who lead I'll  just go back in my history I was  commissioner at the one double-a level  and you saw migration steadily for four  to eight to 16 to 24 so I think there  will always be pressure on increasing  the number but there has to be a balance  of that conversation right now the  feeling is we've struck that balance  with the knowledge that there's always  going to be tension around who is in and  who is left out but if I had a team  let's say and all five of the power  conferences are represented and then I  had three at large after that I don't  want to add more games and I don't know  if we can get around the conference  championship game or if you if you have  that I just think this weekend would be  unbelievable if you started the playoffs  this weekend and you had right eight  versus one yeah Notre Dame against Ohio  State like I think college football's  missing out on storylines Greg yeah you  know I just do we have marvelous  storylines in fact some of the  storylines I wish I could just not pay  attention to that let's just go back  substantively okay from the Southeastern  Conference perspective we were the first  to have a conference championship game  ours is one versus four that's not an  infrequent high-level game for us  we think it's special and it becomes the  issue of what is the gift what where do  you where do you give where do you yield  and I was not in the Commissioner share  when the college football playoff was  created but the reality that we have to  acknowledge is many of my universities  go right into final exams next week we  still have a bowl system that from our  perspective works it's evolving we work  to conclude things prior to the start of  the spring semester so that Monday  championship game date is intentional we  also have dynamics with holidays and NFL  games and could something someday fit  sure but the discussion of what's the  give what what do we give up do we give  up a regular-season games will  accommodate four more teams that seems  unwise for what college football means  to our campuses and our communities and  frankly to the participants because our  student-athletes were clearly rather  play 12 and 11 we went to the standard  C's and so it is it is there's more  complexity there are more pieces to that  conversation than maybe a parent would  just go to eight and I'll tell you if  you ever went to eight the next question  is when you're gonna go I know that  every every bracket exists that's why  we're in a start-up of four that's  worked pretty well but Commissioner it  feels like money Trump's everything here  whether we admit to it or not you know  the bottom line and you know everybody  it feels like that we're increasing they  be a number of teams that can make the  playoffs or do make the playoffs where  is college football what do you have  three percent of the teams they're gonna  make a playoff the NFL has thirty seven  percent of those teams making the  playoffs and I know you're gonna say  well we have bowl games okay those are  nice but these these other you know  leagues these other sports you actually  get a chance to play for a championship  you only have four schools to get a  chance to play yeah that puts great rate  on the regular season so I won't say we  just have all games how about that deal  I will say that some of those NFL teams  run into the playoffs with what nine and  seven records eight and eight records  yeah when you walk through my  all season this year the SEC for the  first time in college football playoff  history as a conference with eight teams  in the top 25 there's a rigor in our  schedule there's an intensity around our  competition that sometimes boils over  but I think that provides those  storylines and in great great meaning  even into early November where people  still have opportunities perhaps to move  up you know one of the oddities that  we're dealing with in fact I was fully  prepared for this question so I'll just  tea it up as you see just repeats you  know Alabama's been in this position  each year the playoff Clemson's moved  into that position and does that cause  people does that circumstance cause  people to view things differently that's  one of those again rhetorical questions  I ask myself but we ought to think about  something like that  but if I said if I showed you data where  the fans wanted this let's say 80% of  the fans say let's have a team play does  that matter at all to use the  Commissioner well I think about that but  that's not the only deciding factors  earlier it was it was about the money  all it was about the money just maybe  expand and figure out how much money is  there it's it is though about college  football being special we've got we have  a unique approach I think these  conference championship games provide  storylines even if it's not a  one-in-four matchup  you know Texas and Oklahoma playing you  have northwestern playing for a Big Ten  championship game and the the amount of  attention on college football this  weekend is increased because of  conference championship games your  follow up will be but would need even be  greater well now you say let's get a  ques two five conference champions when  we were creating things we had some  teams and some of those are that way  this year that might you know some teams  in conference championship games aren't  ranked up just yeah there are we gonna  put it on ranked team that happens to  win a conference championship game  automatically into the playoffs  that's a very different approach than we  have with the four best teams as  established right now well it took a  long time for me to convince all of  these coaches that you know the BCS is  nice but if you go to four teams  it could be nicer so you know that I  mean Notre Dame would be out they'd be  undefeated and they would be out like  like Auburn was you know a decade and a  half ago right you know so we got to for  when nobody wanted to go to four and I  remember all of these coaches I'd talked  to and say you know let's change the BCS  now it'd be Clemson in Alabama but  there'd be no drama to the college  football season like I want to I want to  add a little bit more drama to this  maybe it ends up Clemson and Alabama but  if I you can own December I believe and  that may be true I would counter though  there's an incredible level of drama  around college football now and and you  can imagine I live in my own world or  maybe outside the eleven states of the  SEC the dramas at a different level and  I say that with a smile and great  affection for the intensity what might  change I don't I don't think we've ever  seen circumstances where a boom you just  change a bracket and there's no other  dominoes that follow and so we go back  to principles I talked about that  whether one wants to be cynical or not  we're important we honor the ability for  conferences to schedule differently so  that's a point of controversy now we  want the playoff completed before the  spring academic semester starts we honor  the conference championship games we do  provide a break in December and a piece  of that is intentional because we do  have young men who are graduating and we  have young men who have final exams to  take I also from my my past life watched  both the physical and the personnel poll  on just adding games and that goes back  to watching a 16 in playoff format and I  I am sensitive magnifying  that dynamic because the physical  intensity around Southeastern Conference  football is is significant and adding to  that in December as long we ought to  think about carefully before just yeah I  I'm with you on that I don't want to be  adding games but you know like if you  can have nine conference games for  everybody I mean there was a point  though Greg when you didn't have all the  conference's have a conference title  game like it it's constantly moving it  feels like and I think in five years  from now if we have a conversation I  think we're having a different  conversation but I do understand a lot  of the things that you're pointing out I  just think if you look at the  hypothetical to it I think the  possibilities are a lot of fun I don't  want to get to 16  I don't want to go there I don't want to  get to 12 but I do want to give like  Central Florida deserve to least be in  the conversation last year I thought  that they were a very good team and  maybe this year as well but to have that  possibility that's what you want in all  sports is the possibility that's why we  love March Madness and you don't have  that with college football that's what I  would like to see eight teams maybe you  get an at-large we're a Boise State  years ago or Central Florida you know  that's that's what I would like to have  I'd like to have a little bit more of  that and have these storylines and maybe  it comes down to Alabama and Clemson for  the national title and it probably will  and the good news is there are  thoughtful people involved in the  conversation and you you kind of put a  milestone out there which was Auburn's  undefeated season and I'm not looking at  the calendar I think it 2004 or you know  there was another ten years before there  was the kind of change that were proof  was pursued in the aftermath of that  circumstance so in real time it seems  the pace of consideration may be slow  there are reasons and I think still good  reasons to remain at four but you know  the future is the future and right now I  was pleased to see two SEC teams ranked  in those top four if Nick Saban calls  you right now is it a good thing or a  bad thing  that's why I talked to him with with  some regularity not frequency and those  are always pretty straightforward  conversations whether I'm delivering a  message sure he is and with all my  coaches I talked at 3:00 yesterday have  that positive relationships and  conversations always good if you could  go to one sec tailgate and you got to be  honest Greg yeah I would be an old  Oxford no that's the right answer now if  you if you ask me like we're game venue  in Baton Rouge the Alabama LSU game this  year was incredible well the atmosphere  was the game wasn't your football  tactician it's fascinating  Ole Miss by the way never loses a  tailgate that's the one thing that they  go undefeated in we've got a lot of  special places so before I get myself in  too much trouble a 14 favorite tailgate  now of course you do thanks for joining  us Greg we appreciate your time and have  fun this weekend I appreciate the  invitation would be a great day on  Saturday that's Greg Sankey SEC  Commissioner for more Dan Patrick show  to the audience Channel 239 on DirecTV  or download the Dan Patrick show app  [Music]

